[[Holy Armor]] is a legendary [[Armor]] available in the shop to all classes. It's generally stronger than the [[Leather Armor]], granting more {{icon/block}} and with a stronger cleansing ability (although it only works on {{icon/poison}}). It also can grant a lot of {{icon/regeneration}} if multiple [[Holy]] items are placed next to it.

There are multiple strong crafts for the [[Holy Armor]].

When combined with a [[Corrupted Crystal]], the [[Holy Armor]] becomes [[Corrupted Armor]], which grants much more {{icon/block}}, protects debuffs on the opponent from being cleansed, and cleanses the player's own debuffs to put them on the opponent.

When combined with a [[Mana Orb]], the [[Holy Armor]] becomes the [[Moon Armor]], which grants large amounts of {{icon/mana}} and reflects debuffs. It can also gain a large amount of armor if many [[Magic]] items are placed around it.

Pyromancers can use two [[Flame]]s to turn the [[Holy Armor]] into [[Sun Armor]], which isn't a massive improvement, but spends {{icon/heat}} to cleanse and heal, and gains {{icon/heat}} from adjacent [[Holy]] or [[Fire]] items.

Combining the [[Holy Armor]] with either a [[Bunch of Coins]] or a [[Maneki-neko]], will grant the [[Gold armor]], which is superior in almost every way, granting more {{icon/block}}, more {{icon/regeneration}}, cleansing more and a wider variety of debuffs, and even granting 3 {{icon/gold}} per turn, although it has the possibly significant drawback of making all the player's weapons attack much slower.

Crafting any Collar item ([[Acorn Collar]] and its derivatives) with [[Holy Armor]] will convert the Collar into a [[White Lily Collar]] without consuming the [[Holy Armor]].
